BT /F2 10 Tf 54 692 Td (PROBLEM) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 678 Td (Find the contiguous subarray with the greatest sum.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 658 Td (ALGORITHM) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 644 Td (Recursively find the best subarray in the left half and right half. Also compute the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 631 Td (    best crossing sum from the middle, then take the maximum of the three.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 611 Td (PSEUDOCODE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 597 Td (best\(A, lo, hi\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 584 Td (    if lo == hi: return A[lo]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 571 Td (    mid = \(lo + hi\) // 2) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 558 Td (    return max\(best\(left\), best\(right\), best_crossing\(A, lo, mid, hi\)\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 538 Td (EXAMPLE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 524 Td (For [-2,1,-3,4,-1,2,1,-5,4], the maximum-sum subarray is [4,-1,2,1] with sum 6.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 504 Td (COMPLEXITY) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 490 Td (The recurrence is T\(n\) = 2T\(n/2\) + O\(n\), giving O\(n log n\) time and O\(log n\) recursion) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 477 Td (    depth.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 457 Td (NOTE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 443 Td (Kadane's algorithm solves the same problem in O\(n\) time, but this exercise demonstrates) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 430 Td (    divide and conquer.) Tj ET
